  "answer": "According to current web sources (retrieved October 27, 2026), boiling begins when the atmospheric pressure equals the vapor pressure of the liquid [W2]. \n\nAt the summit of Mount Everest (elevation 8,848 m / 29,029 ft), atmospheric pressure drops to approximately 33.7 to 34 kPa (about 255 Torr) [W1, W2]. Because of this lower pressure, water needs to reach approximately 69.9 °C to 71 °C (about 158 °F to 160 °F) before it boils [W1, W2, W3]."
}